1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,952
For twenty-seven years, nobody was
charged with killing Tupac Shakur.

2
00:00:05,219 --> 00:00:08,920
This summer, it took a jury less
than three hours to convict.

3
00:00:09,189 --> 00:00:13,063
The man they convicted is
Duane Davis, known as Keffe D.

4
00:00:13,802 --> 00:00:16,894
Prosecutors never said
he pulled the trigger.

5
00:00:17,365 --> 00:00:20,599
They said he planned the
shooting, and supplied the gun.

6
00:00:21,244 --> 00:00:25,229
And the heart of the case,
prosecutors said, was his own words.

7
00:00:25,708 --> 00:00:28,370
A police interview in 2008.

8
00:00:28,797 --> 00:00:29,934
Television.

9
00:00:30,303 --> 00:00:33,712
Even a memoir, in which
he told the story himself.

10
00:00:34,556 --> 00:00:38,539
Now he says he only told those
stories because he was paid.

11
00:00:39,110 --> 00:00:42,595
On the thirteenth of October,
he's due to be sentenced.

12
00:00:42,963 --> 00:00:46,369
He faces up to life in
prison, without parole.

13
00:00:46,785 --> 00:00:50,344
This is how a thirty-year-old
case finally reached a verdict,

14
00:00:50,344 --> 00:00:52,787
and what the record still can't tell us.

15
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:54,471
Las Vegas.

16
00:00:54,795 --> 00:00:58,029
The seventh of September, 1996.

17
00:00:58,303 --> 00:01:02,608
Tupac Shakur had been at a
boxing match at the MGM Grand.

18
00:01:02,965 --> 00:01:06,746
Prosecutors later told the jury
that earlier that night, Tupac,

19
00:01:06,746 --> 00:01:10,910
Suge Knight and their group had
beaten up Davis's nephew in the hotel.

20
00:01:11,747 --> 00:01:14,389
His name was Orlando Anderson.

21
00:01:15,008 --> 00:01:18,362
A few hours later, at about
a quarter past eleven,

22
00:01:18,362 --> 00:01:21,956
Tupac was riding in the
passenger seat of a black BMW.

23
00:01:22,269 --> 00:01:26,042
Suge Knight, the head of Death
Row Records, was driving.

24
00:01:26,433 --> 00:01:30,757
They stopped at a red light,
near Flamingo Road and Koval Lane.

25
00:01:31,176 --> 00:01:33,946
A white Cadillac pulled up alongside.

26
00:01:34,806 --> 00:01:37,732
Someone inside it opened fire.

27
00:01:38,375 --> 00:01:41,086
Tupac was hit several times.

28
00:01:41,441 --> 00:01:44,353
Knight survived, with minor injuries.

29
00:01:44,839 --> 00:01:48,146
Six days later, on the
thirteenth of September,

30
00:01:48,146 --> 00:01:51,453
Tupac Shakur died at
University Medical Center.

31
00:01:52,197 --> 00:01:54,712
Anderson denied any involvement.

32
00:01:55,067 --> 00:01:59,571
In 1998, he died in an
unrelated shooting in Compton.

33
00:01:59,872 --> 00:02:01,481
He was never charged.

34
00:02:01,858 --> 00:02:03,363
Years went by.

35
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:05,396
Then decades.

36
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:07,814
Nobody was charged.

37
00:02:08,570 --> 00:02:13,202
In 2018, Las Vegas police said
it was still an open homicide.

38
00:02:13,628 --> 00:02:17,089
But one man said, again and
again, that he'd been there.

39
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:18,758
Duane Davis.

40
00:02:19,052 --> 00:02:21,750
Police and prosecutors
said he was a former

41
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:24,227
leader of the South Side Compton Crips.

42
00:02:24,541 --> 00:02:29,391
In 2008, he sat down with a federal
and local task force investigating the

43
00:02:29,391 --> 00:02:32,786
killing, led by Los Angeles
detective Greg Kading.

44
00:02:33,091 --> 00:02:36,869
It was what's called a proffer,
or a 'queen for a day' interview.

45
00:02:37,297 --> 00:02:39,761
And Davis told them a story.

46
00:02:40,276 --> 00:02:43,392
He said he was in the front
passenger seat of the Cadillac,

47
00:02:43,392 --> 00:02:45,981
and that he handed a gun
to the men in the back.

48
00:02:46,904 --> 00:02:52,177
And he named the man he said fired the
shots: his own nephew, Orlando Anderson.

49
00:02:52,869 --> 00:02:57,153
Anderson had denied any involvement,
and he was never charged.

50
00:02:57,619 --> 00:03:00,557
By then, he had been dead for a decade.

51
00:03:01,204 --> 00:03:04,367
Ten years later, Davis went on television.

52
00:03:04,764 --> 00:03:08,598
He said the shots came from the
back seat of the car he was in.

53
00:03:09,038 --> 00:03:11,335
But he wouldn't say who fired.

54
00:03:11,737 --> 00:03:14,114
His stories didn't always match.

55
00:03:14,419 --> 00:03:17,534
In one interview, he said he
ducked when the shooting started,

56
00:03:17,534 --> 00:03:19,274
and didn't know who had the gun.

57
00:03:19,653 --> 00:03:24,310
Then, in 2019, he published a
memoir, Compton Street Legend.

58
00:03:24,668 --> 00:03:29,001
In it, he said he was in the Cadillac,
and passed the gun into the back seat.

59
00:03:29,493 --> 00:03:32,676
He never claimed to have
fired a shot himself.

60
00:03:33,322 --> 00:03:37,881
In July 2023, Las Vegas police
searched a home in Henderson, Nevada,

61
00:03:37,881 --> 00:03:39,237
linked to Davis.

62
00:03:39,610 --> 00:03:42,472
Two months later, on the
twenty-ninth of September,

63
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:45,886
police arrested him near his home,
while he was out on a walk.

64
00:03:46,332 --> 00:03:50,459
A grand jury had indicted him
for murder, with a deadly weapon.

65
00:03:50,817 --> 00:03:55,780
District Attorney Steve Wolfson said:
"Today, we are taking that first step."

66
00:03:56,507 --> 00:03:58,769
Davis pleaded not guilty.

67
00:03:59,074 --> 00:04:02,026
Prosecutors did not
seek the death penalty.

68
00:04:02,332 --> 00:04:04,518
He was never released on bail.

69
00:04:04,812 --> 00:04:09,245
In 2024, the judge refused to accept
bail money put up by a rap manager,

70
00:04:09,245 --> 00:04:12,768
finding it hadn't been shown
to come from legal sources.

71
00:04:13,112 --> 00:04:17,554
His lawyers argued he'd been
promised immunity, back in 2008.

72
00:04:17,885 --> 00:04:20,998
The judge found no proof
of any immunity deal.

73
00:04:21,703 --> 00:04:26,888
And in July 2026, Judge Carli Kierny
ruled that the jury could hear the 2008

74
00:04:26,888 --> 00:04:30,113
interview, and refused
to exclude the memoir.

75
00:04:30,552 --> 00:04:33,814
She found Davis had adopted
the book as his own.

76
00:04:34,379 --> 00:04:37,742
The trial opened in August 2026.

77
00:04:38,202 --> 00:04:41,026
Prosecutors told jurors Davis
didn't pull the trigger,

78
00:04:41,026 --> 00:04:44,602
but that he planned the shooting,
in revenge for his nephew's beating,

79
00:04:44,602 --> 00:04:45,873
and supplied the gun.

80
00:04:46,275 --> 00:04:49,701
His defence said he'd made up
or embellished his stories,

81
00:04:49,701 --> 00:04:51,333
for money and notoriety.

82
00:04:51,646 --> 00:04:53,486
That nothing backed them up.

83
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:55,936
That the gun was never found.

84
00:04:56,648 --> 00:04:59,647
His own lawyer told the
jury that Davis was, quote,

85
00:04:59,647 --> 00:05:02,172
'full of crap' when he told those stories.

86
00:05:02,757 --> 00:05:07,351
Suge Knight, who survived the shooting,
was on the prosecution's witness list.

87
00:05:07,606 --> 00:05:09,173
He was never called.

88
00:05:09,603 --> 00:05:12,938
Of the four men prosecutors
say were in the Cadillac,

89
00:05:12,938 --> 00:05:15,199
Davis is the only one still alive.

90
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:18,064
Davis did not testify.

91
00:05:18,339 --> 00:05:21,892
His defence rested after
calling three witnesses.

92
00:05:22,226 --> 00:05:25,267
In his closing argument,
prosecutor Binu Palal

93
00:05:25,267 --> 00:05:27,958
said Davis got a gun and 'went hunting'.

94
00:05:28,326 --> 00:05:31,012
"It's a plan," he said, "not an impulse."

95
00:05:31,857 --> 00:05:35,887
On the thirty-first of August,
2026, after less than three hours,

96
00:05:35,887 --> 00:05:40,711
the jury found Duane Davis guilty of
first-degree murder, with a deadly weapon.

97
00:05:41,353 --> 00:05:46,457
Tupac's sister, Sekyiwa Shakur,
cried, and hugged the prosecutors.

98
00:05:46,991 --> 00:05:50,204
The family said it was
elated, and relieved.

99
00:05:51,009 --> 00:05:55,515
The verdict came one week before the
thirtieth anniversary of the shooting.

100
00:05:56,223 --> 00:05:59,258
Davis told the judge he wanted to appeal.

101
00:05:59,587 --> 00:06:02,141
He'll be able to, once he's sentenced.

102
00:06:02,512 --> 00:06:04,790
And he now says he's innocent.

103
00:06:05,210 --> 00:06:10,264
In a jailhouse interview with ABC, he said
he only confessed because he was paid.

104
00:06:10,706 --> 00:06:13,261
After the verdict, he told The Hollywood

105
00:06:13,261 --> 00:06:16,261
Reporter he wasn't even
in Las Vegas that night.

106
00:06:16,757 --> 00:06:19,997
Three times over the years,
he said he was there.

107
00:06:20,472 --> 00:06:22,390
Now he says he wasn't.

108
00:06:23,161 --> 00:06:27,890
Davis has been held in the Clark County
Detention Center since his arrest.

109
00:06:28,636 --> 00:06:33,342
On the thirteenth of October,
2026, he's due to be sentenced.

110
00:06:33,701 --> 00:06:37,940
He faces up to life in prison,
without the possibility of parole.

111
00:06:38,518 --> 00:06:43,074
After the verdict, the district attorney
said there still isn't enough evidence to

112
00:06:43,074 --> 00:06:44,368
charge anyone else.

113
00:06:45,144 --> 00:06:47,779
So, here's where the record stands.

114
00:06:48,437 --> 00:06:55,075
Tupac Shakur was shot in Las Vegas in
September 1996, and died six days later.

115
00:06:55,733 --> 00:06:59,248
Duane Davis is the only
person ever charged.

116
00:06:59,744 --> 00:07:03,265
A jury convicted him
of first-degree murder.

117
00:07:03,746 --> 00:07:06,757
Prosecutors never said he fired the gun.

118
00:07:07,398 --> 00:07:10,712
He says he's innocent,
and he plans to appeal.

119
00:07:11,175 --> 00:07:16,127
And the man he once named as the shooter,
Orlando Anderson, denied any involvement,

120
00:07:16,127 --> 00:07:17,685
and was never charged.
